## 1. Scope

This audit covers saga definitions, execution, compensation, retries, checkpoints, state machines, UI support, and worker integration. It inspects `packages/product-platform/src/product_platform/runtime/sagas.py`, `saga_executor.py`, `saga_actions.py`, `0021_saga_builder.up.sql`, saga routes in `api/app.py`, `packages/agent-hypervisor/src/hypervisor/saga`, and runtime UI. Relevant benchmarks are Temporal workflows, LangGraph durable execution, and enterprise compensation/recovery patterns. Out of scope: general worker queue reliability, covered in WRK.

## 2. Current Implementation Summary

Product Platform has saga builder persistence in `0021_saga_builder.up.sql`, saga models in `runtime/models.py`, a limited executable state model in `runtime/sagas.py`, demo-safe action execution in `runtime/saga_executor.py`, and predefined demo actions in `runtime/saga_actions.py`. API routes support validation, execution, monitor data, and compensation around `api/app.py:9278` to `api/app.py:9364`. The frontend runtime page renders saga forms and execution views. The older hypervisor package has `SagaOrchestrator` and checkpoint scaffolding under `packages/agent-hypervisor/src/hypervisor/saga`.

Current workflow: users define saga-like workflows, execute demo-safe actions, see status, and trigger compensation for supported records. The flow does not provide deterministic replay, persisted checkpoints, reliable compensation queues, or a production activity boundary.

