## 7. Feature-Level Target State

Sagas should use a single durable state machine with persisted event history, checkpoints, idempotent activities, compensation attempts, worker leases, and manual repair states. Data models should represent steps, attempts, compensation records, checkpoints, and external operation IDs. APIs should expose state and repair actions without executing side effects inline. Workers should execute typed activities with retry, heartbeat, and timeout semantics. UI should show step timeline, compensation status, and manual intervention tasks. Tests should prove crash recovery, replay, idempotency, and compensation failure handling.
